Subject: logout-greeter: list boot entries with kdos-bootctl

The logout screen names the boot entry the next restart switches to. It
reads the entry's id from login1's RebootToBootLoaderEntry and looks up
its title in the output of `bootctl list --json=short`. KDOS installs no
program called bootctl: its A/B slots are listed by
`kdos-bootctl list --json=short`, which prints the same JSON shape, one
entry per slot. Without the change the lookup finds no program and the
screen shows no entry.

--- a/logout-greeter/shutdowndlg.cpp
+++ b/logout-greeter/shutdowndlg.cpp
@@ -191,7 +191,7 @@
 
             const QStringList bootctlArgs{u"list"_s, u"--json=short"_s};
 
-            bootctl->start(u"bootctl"_s, bootctlArgs);
+            bootctl->start(u"kdos-bootctl"_s, bootctlArgs);
         });
     }
 
